========================================================================================
P1  THE SHEET: rho_dark = A/r^2  ->  Sigma_dark(R) = pi A/R  (exact LOS integral)
========================================================================================
    A = sqrt(G M_b a0)/(4 pi G) = 3.516711e+19 kg/m   (M_b = 7e+10 Msun, a0 canonical)
    Sigma_dark(R0, full LOS) = pi A/R0 =   209.0 Msun/pc^2   (the sheet TOTAL;
        NOT the survey number -- G078's committed self-correction)
    Sigma_dark(R0, A/R shorthand) =    66.5 Msun/pc^2   (un-pi'd form, stated)
    Sigma_dark(R0, +/- 1.1 kpc window) =    17.7 Msun/pc^2   (the survey-measurable column)
    rho_dark(R0) = A/R0^2 = 0.0081 Msun/pc^3   (measured 0.008-0.015; G078: 0.0081)
    Sigma_b(R0) ~ 35-50 Msun/pc^2
    -> the local dark:baryon surface ratios:
         full-LOS  : 4.18-5.97   (sheet total; not the survey reading)
         A/R form  : 1.33-1.90   (shorthand; not the survey reading)
         survey    : 0.35-0.51   (finite +/-1.1 kpc column vs Sigma_b)
         volume    : 0.246   (A/R0^2 vs stellar 0.033 -- the density reading)
    measured dark:stellar band: 0.008-0.015 vs 0.033+/-0.004 -> [0.24, 0.45] nominal, [0.22, 0.52] with the stellar spread
    measured local dark COLUMN band (G078): 15-25 Msun/pc^2 in the +/-1.1 kpc window
  [PASS] V1 [sheet ratio] the SURVEY reading -- Sigma_dark(R0)/Sigma_b(R0) with the finite +/-1.1 kpc column -- lands in the measured dark:stellar band (0.008-0.015 vs 0.033)
         measured: survey ratio 0.35-0.51 vs measured [0.24, 0.45] ([0.22, 0.52] with stellar +/-0.004); column 17.7 in [15, 25]; overlap 0.10
         reading : G078's corrected reading, restated: the full-LOS total 209.0 and the A/R shorthand (66.5) are NOT the survey numbers (their ratios 4.2-6.0 and 1.33-1.90 overshoot the band); the finite +/-1.1 kpc column IS the survey reading and it sits in the band (ratio 0.35-0.51, inside [0.22, 0.52] with the stellar spread, top edge vs the nominal band). The same law's volume form A/R0^2 = 0.0081 -> ratio 0.246, in the measured band at the lower edge.

